{#- AP CAP — HD-312 guest turn-up DELTA: CAP bridge VLAN 30 (2026-09-03).
    Once CAPsMAN provisions 'Kogler guest' on the 5GHz radio, the CAP dynamically creates
    a slave interface (wifi* on the 5GHz radio) whose SSID is cfg-kogler-guest. The slave
    needs a bridge VLAN-30 entry so its frames get tagged on the ether1 uplink (matching
    the live Kogler=10 / IOT=20 pattern). Run AFTER the router provisioning change +
    after the slave appears (check /interface wifi on the AP).
    Idempotent: guarded — safe to re-import.
    NOTE: the slave interface name is dynamic (wifi27 on spalnica, wifi8 on dnevna as of
    2026-09-03) — find it by its master SSID 'Kogler guest'. -#}
# =============================================================================
# HD-312 guest — AP CAP bridge VLAN 30 DELTA (apply per AP: ap-spalnica, ap-dnevna)
# =============================================================================

# Find the 5GHz slave interface that carries cfg-kogler-guest: it is the wifi
# interface whose configuration.ssid == 'Kogler guest' (provisioned slave).
# (mac-address C6:* = locally-administered slave radio MAC; master = wifi2/5GHz.)
:local guestIface ""
:foreach i in=[/interface wifi find where master-interface!="" and configuration.ssid="Kogler guest"] do={
    :set guestIface [/interface wifi get $i name]
}

:if ($guestIface != "") do={
    :if ([/interface bridge port find where bridge=bridge interface=$guestIface] = "") do={
        /interface bridge port add bridge=bridge interface=$guestIface pvid=30
    }
    :if ([/interface bridge vlan find where bridge=bridge vlan-ids=30] = "") do={
        /interface bridge vlan add bridge=bridge vlan-ids=30 tagged=ether1 untagged=$guestIface
    }
} else={
    :put "HD-312 ap delta: no wifi slave with SSID 'Kogler guest' yet — provisioning may still be in progress"
}

# ---- End ----
# Verify: /interface bridge port print (guest slave pvid=30) + /interface bridge vlan print (vlan-ids=30 tagged=ether1)